From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 22:16:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] debian: Build the v4l2request hwdecs

Enable the v4l2request hwdec/interop added by the preceding patches
(https://github.com/mpv-player/mpv/pull/14690). It needs an FFmpeg with the
V4L2 Request API hwdevice (AV_HWDEVICE_TYPE_V4L2REQUEST); use "enabled" so
the build fails rather than silently dropping it.

Ubuntu's /etc/mpv/mpv.conf (hwdec=vaapi) is left as it is: on boards whose
decoders are V4L2 stateless devices the VA-API driver over V4L2
(v4l2-request-va-driver) serves hwdec=vaapi, and hwdec=auto/auto-copy
(what libmpv front ends such as Jellyfin Desktop ask for) reach
v4l2request through the auto-probe whitelist patch.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 debian/rules | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/debian/rules b/debian/rules
index b52e7ea..6923f04 100755
--- a/debian/rules
+++ b/debian/rules
@@ -17,6 +17,7 @@ override_dh_auto_configure:
 		-Dbuild-date=false \
 		-Dcdda=enabled \
 		-Ddvdnav=enabled \
+		-Dv4l2request=enabled \
 		$(ARCH_CONFIGURE)
 
 execute_after_dh_auto_install:
